Moody Centre station is an intermodal rapid transit station in Metro Vancouver served by both the Millennium Line — part of the SkyTrain system — and the region &apos;s West Coast Express commuter rail system . It is located in Port Moody , British Columbia , on the south side of the Canadian Pacific Railway ( CPR ) tracks , at the north foot of Williams Street , approximately 200 metres ( 660 ft ) north of St. John &apos;s Street .
Moody Centre replaced the previous Port Moody station on the West Coast Express . The new station opened on December 2 , 2016 , along with the rest of the Evergreen Extension .
Station information .
