The 12269 / 70 Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station - Hazrat Nizamuddin Duronto Express is a Superfast express train of the Duronto Express category belonging to Indian Railways - Southern Railway zone that runs between Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station and Hazrat Nizamuddin in India .
It operates as train number 12269 from Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station to Hazrat Nizamuddin and as train number 12270 in the reverse direction serving the states of Tamil Nadu , Andhra Pradesh , Maharashtra , Madhya Pradesh , Uttar Pradesh &amp; amp ; Delhi .
It was part of the Duronto Express series of trains introduced by the then railway minister of India Ms. Mamata Banerjee in the 2009-10 railway budget
Coaches .
The 12269 / 70 Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station - Hazrat Nizamuddin Duronto Express presently has 1 AC 1st Class , 2 AC 2 tier , 4 AC 3 tier , 8 Sleeper Class &amp; amp ; 2 End on Generator Coaches . In addition , it also carries a Pantry car coach .
As is customary with most train services in India , Coach Composition may be amended at the discretion of Indian Railways depending on demand .
Service .
The 12269 Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station - Hazrat Nizamuddin Duronto Express covers the distance of in 27 hours 55 mins averaging &amp; amp ; in 28 hours 55 mins as 12270 Hazrat Nizamuddin - Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station Duronto Express averaging .
As the average speed of the train is above , as per Indian Railway rules , its fare includes a Superfast surcharge .
Routeing .
The 12269 / 70 Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station - Hazrat Nizamuddin Duronto Express runs from Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station via Vijayawada Junction , Balharshah Junction , Nagpur , Bhopal Habibganj Railway Station , Jhansi Junction , Gwalior to Hazrat Nizamuddin .
Traction .
As the route is fully electrified , it is an end to end haul by a Royapuram or Erode based Head on Generation enabled WAP 7 .
Timings .
12269 Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station - Hazrat Nizamuddin Duronto Express leaves Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station every Monday &amp; amp ; Friday reaching Hazrat Nizamuddin the next day .
12270 Hazrat Nizamuddin - Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station Duronto Express leaves Hazrat Nizamuddin every Tuesday &amp; amp ; Saturday reaching Puratchi Thalaivar Dr. M.G. Ramachandran Central Railway Station the next day .
Niranjanapur or Niranjanpur is a village in the Bidhuna tehsil of Auraiya District in Uttar Pradesh , India .
History .
On 17 September 1997 two tehsils named Auraiya and Bidhuna were separated from district Etawah to form the new district named as Auraiya . Since then Niranjanapur falls in the territory of District Auraiya .
Geography .
Niranjanapur lies in the south-western portion of Uttar Pradesh 26 ° 38 ′ 41 ″ N 79 ° 34 ′ 54 ″ E and also is a part of Kanpur Division . The village is situated in the central doab region of District Auraiya in the state of Uttar Pradesh . It is situated 5 kilometers north-east of town Dibiyapur .
It covers an area of 1.19 km2 ( 0.46 sq mi ) , of which more than one-third ( 78.65 hectares ) is irrigated area . Though the village lacks in any flow water body , but it does contain 3 ponds , few wells &amp; amp ; tubewells .
Climate .
The Village features an atypical version of the humid subtropical climate . Summers are long and the weather is extremely hot from early April to mid-October , with the monsoon season in between . The average annual rainfall in the region is 792 mm . About 85 % of the annual normal rainfall in the region is received during the south west monsoon months from June to September , August being the rainiest month . The brief , mild winter starts in late November , peaks in January and heavy fog often occurs .
Land .
Total Area of the village is 119 hectares . The area of cultivable land in the village is 78.65 hectares .
Architecture .
The architecture of the houses is original and unique . Most of them are built with mud , but there are also new houses , using bricks &amp; amp ; cement .
Population .
According to 2011 census of India the population of the village is 630 . Among these 334 are males &amp; amp ; 296 are females . The sex ratio of the village is 886 females per 1,000 men . Since the end of the 20th century the population has decreased very quickly . Most of the inhabitants went to the bigger towns and cities . Few houses have been abandoned and began to self-demolish .
Transport .
The Village is well equipped with road as it is being the major way of transportation in the region . Nearest Major town , Dibiyapur is at 6 km distance .
